# missingmed — Missing-data causal mediation (R package, mediationverse)
# Scope decided 2026-06-04 (Data-Wise/missingmed#1): general CRAN-targeted toolkit —
# MI + IPW estimators, SEM + GLM models, MAR + MNAR sensitivity. S7-first.
# Thin orchestration layer: fit via medfit, infer via rmediation, simulate via medsim.

## Since v0.2.0 (unreleased work on dev)
- 2026-08-22 (merged): PR #5 feature/glm-phase -> dev (24fffc3). Also merged
  rforge#75 (ac16b0a), the .STATUS frontmatter parser fix. Two CI failures were
  self-inflicted by running a SUBSET of what CI runs: rforge's gate is
  tests/test-all.sh (44 checks), not `pytest tests/` (599); and missingmed's
  pkgdown job reads _pkgdown.yml's explicit reference index, which R CMD check
  never opens — two new exports were missing from it. See CLAUDE.md.
- 2026-08-30 (release): v0.3.1 SHIPPED — tag 2f466de, GitHub release published,
  main CI green (R-CMD-check + pkgdown). Patch of 7 correctness fixes. Suite
  128 -> 200 across the day; check --as-cran 0/0/0 throughout. r-universe still
  served 0.3.0 at close: it polls main and the v0.3.0 cycle took ~96 min from
  merge to published, so expect 0.3.1 within a couple of hours. Not a fault.
- 2026-08-30 (process): THREE adversarial reviews ran, and two of them caught
  regressions introduced by the PREVIOUS round of fixes — maxit = 0 returning a
  silently flat sensitivity curve, and .mm_drop_path() turning log(Y) ~ . into
  Y ~ . so the two log-likelihoods were on different scales and T was not a
  likelihood ratio (measured 813.76, p = 1.3e-32, rejecting unconditionally).
  Neither would have surfaced from a failing test. See memory
  green-ci-is-not-evidence-of-a-correct-artifact.
- 2026-08-30 (release): v0.3.0 SHIPPED — tag v0.3.0 on e482527, GitHub release
  published, main CI green, docs live. rforge cran-prep caught what
  R CMD check --as-cran cannot see: VignetteBuilder declared knitr while the
  engine is knitr::rmarkdown, so CRAN's noSuggests pass ERRORed on vignette
  rebuilding. Fixed before tagging.
- 2026-08-30 (docs): vignettes/technical.Rmd enriched to the self-study standard
  — five base-R teaching figures, a hand-authored static pipeline SVG (the
  mermaid fence rendered as raw escaped text; neither html_vignette nor pkgdown
  loads mermaid.js, and the first render gate passed on the literal word
  "mermaid"), worked examples, folded self-checks. Verified on the BUILT site,
  not just the vignette.
- 2026-08-30 (fix): three correctness fixes now on dev, unreleased at time of
  writing. MBCO constrained models nulled only the main effect, so
  Y ~ poly(M,2) + X left the constrained model IDENTICAL to the full one — T = 0,
  p = 1, the test could never reject. infer() ignored @conf_level: asking for 90%
  silently returned a 95% interval, 19.7% wider. pool() presented imputation 1's
  @data/@sigma_m/@sigma_y as pooled. Specs: SPEC-mbco-constrained-models-2026-08-30.md
  (CLOSED, author ruled reading (i)), PLAN-parked-findings-2026-08-30.md (item 3
  deferred). Adversarial review of the latter caught %||% resolving from base
  (R >= 4.4.0 only, DESCRIPTION allows 4.1.0 — would have failed oldrel CI) and a
  blanking strategy medfit's validator rejects outright.
- 2026-08-30 (review + gate): PR #7 merged (3521d91). Two adversarial review
  passes over the release candidate found 4 blockers, then 5 more in the fixes
  themselves -- including a REGRESSION introduced by the first pass: passing
  maxit = mids$iteration made a maxit = 0 baseline return a silently FLAT
  sensitivity curve. Confirmed defects, all fixed: IPW weights misaligned to
  rows (fitted() vs predict()); .mnar_reimpute() dropping maxit/blocks/formulas/
  ignore; pool() masking mice::pool; mids$method being block-keyed not
  variable-keyed; mice floor needing >= 3.18.0 for $calltype.
  Then rforge cran-prep caught what R CMD check --as-cran cannot see:
  VignetteBuilder declared knitr but the engine is knitr::rmarkdown, so the
  CRAN noSuggests pass ERRORed on vignette rebuilding. Gate now STATUS ready.
  148 tests pass; check --as-cran 0/0/0.
- 2026-08-30 (research): prior-art scan (docs/specs/SPEC-narfcs-delegation-
  2026-08-29.md). Every method component is already published; the package-level
  gap is real -- no R package combines missing-data handling + mediation + MNAR
  sensitivity. Verified empirically that the post-based delta and mice's native
  mnar.norm produce IDENTICAL draws (8.9e-16) on the same seed, which retires
  the old spec's open fork.
- 2026-08-29 (merge): PR #6 MNAR sensitivity MERGED to dev (b9ac0ce). Before the
  merge an adversarial review of the diff found 3 real defects, fixed in 7aa2a9f:
  format() truncated the delta to 7 sig. digits inside the post expression
  (now digits = 15); seed_source said "argument" for the hard-coded fallback
  (now "default"); pmm check + method_target only covered target[1] of a
  multi-column delta (msp is documented as target[1]). 133 pass / 0 fail.
- 2026-08-22 (code): RMediation API audit DONE. The entire runtime surface is
  ci_mediation_data() (R/infer.R:32,56); 1.4.0 -> 1.7.0 is NON-BREAKING because
  pool() already emits named a/b/c_prime + dimnamed vcov, exactly what 1.5.0's
  strict name-based extraction requires. Floor raised to RMediation (>= 1.5.0):
  below it, unresolvable paths silently assumed cov(a,b)=0 -> a wrong CI instead
  of an error. New regression test pins that (test-s7-pipeline.R).
  Evidence: 73 pass / 0 fail / 0 skip vs RMediation 1.7.0, medfit 0.3.2, R 4.6.1.
  NB the installed library was 1.6.1 until this session; 1.7.0 now installed.
  R CMD check --as-cran: Status OK (0E/0W/0N) after .Rbuildignore'ing the
  .token-optimizer dir, which had produced a hidden-files NOTE.
- 2026-08-22 (docs): follow-up plan + per-item outcomes ->
  docs/specs/PLAN-post-v0.2.0-followups-2026-08-22.md. Items 1 and 2 DONE, GLM DONE,
  MNAR not started. That file is the record; do not restate its detail here.
- 2026-08-22 (branch, UNMERGED): feature/glm-phase — GLM phase shipped. Non-gaussian
  families now tested (MI x {binomial mediator, binomial outcome, poisson outcome};
  IPW x {binomial mediator, binomial outcome} with sandwich; MBCO D4 with a binomial
  mediator, previously gaussian-only). NO production code changed — the plan's
  "already plumbed, zero medfit blockers" finding held. 103 pass / 0 fail (was 73),
  R CMD check Status OK. Also on that branch: 6 tidyselect .data$ deprecations fixed,
  and roxygen2 7.3.3 -> 8.0.0 regeneration (matches medfit/medsim/RMediation).
  Documented in vignette("technical") 5A: under a non-identity link a*b is on the
  LINK scale (log-odds, log-rate) — not a risk difference or odds ratio, and
  exp(a*b) is not one either.
- 2026-08-22 (hygiene): removed the stale ORCHESTRATE-s7-migration.md working
  artifact (merge-cleanup rule; content remains in git history).
  Note: /rforge:status could not read this file — its parser keys on emoji section
  headers (🎯 📊 ✅ 📋 ⏰) while all 7 active packages use `key: value` frontmatter.
  Worse than "no data": it took max() over every N% in the prose, so every package
  was reported with a WRONG progress figure. FIXED on rforge
  feature/status-frontmatter (cf3182d, pushed, UNMERGED) — 599 pass / 2 skip.
- 2026-08-22 (branch, UNMERGED): feature/mnar-sensitivity — MNAR phase COMPLETE,
  M1–M6. sensitivity_mnar() + MDSensitivityResult: delta-adjusted imputation over
  a grid, re-running the pipeline per rung to give a sensitivity CURVE (not an
  estimator — MAR vs MNAR is untestable, so no rung is "the MNAR estimate").
  98 tests / 0 fail, R CMD check Status OK. Design record:
  docs/specs/SPEC-mnar-sensitivity-2026-08-22.md +
  docs/research/RESEARCH-mnar-mechanisms-2026-08-22.md.
  Key design facts worth not re-deriving:
    * delta is a CONDITIONAL sensitivity parameter (CSP); what analysts elicit is
      MARGINAL. Confusing them cost coverage 95% -> 49.3% in Tompsett et al.
      (2018). tidy() therefore reports the realized msp beside the supplied delta.
    * Re-imputation rebuilds from the mids' STORED SLOTS, never mids$call, which
      does not resolve outside the function that built the mids.
    * mechanism = "mnar" on set_md_mediation() is now DEPRECATED + ignored; it
      never changed behavior. Only sensitivity_mnar() stamps it.
    * v1 uses mice's `post`; the NARFCS mice extension (moreno-betancur/NARFCS)
      is the v2 direction but is GitHub-only, and delegating loses the delta = 0
      identity (NARFCS also conditions on other variables' missingness).
  Literature is curated in Zotero ("MNAR sensitivity — missingmed", 14 items) and
  in a NotebookLM notebook (13 full-text sources).
- 2026-07-19: .Rbuildignore the .remember/ session-memory dir (5946b3f).
- 2026-07-16: .STATUS gained `kind: package` (ecosystem convention).

## v0.2.0 RELEASED — 2026-06-12 (all integration steps DONE)
# - main = 0.2.0 (PR #3 ipw-phase1->dev, PR #4 dev->main). GitHub release v0.2.0.
#   https://github.com/Data-Wise/missingmed/releases/tag/v0.2.0
# - medfit 0.3.1 + RMediation 1.4.0 live on r-universe (deps satisfied).
# - Feature worktrees + branches (feature/s7-migration, feature/ipw-phase1) merged
#   and DELETED. Only docs/ipw-phase1-spec remains (historical spec).
# - CI fixes that unblocked the release (key learnings):
#     * RMediation remote MUST be name-qualified: RMediation=data-wise/rmediation
#       (repo 'rmediation' != package 'RMediation'); plain form fails pak solve.
#     * DESCRIPTION Additional_repositories = data-wise r-universe (non-CRAN deps).
#     * check.yml modernized off renv::restore() (stale lock -> old rlang fails to
#       compile on R 4.6) to standard r-lib setup-r-dependencies + check-r-package.
#     * RENV_CONFIG_AUTOLOADER_ENABLED=FALSE in CI (keep dev renv out of CI).
# - pkgdown destination = pkgdown-site (docs/ holds specs); deploy via gh-pages.
# - Post-release watch: r-universe rebuild of missingmed 0.2.0 (cron); main CI/site deploy.

